# Response headers for Cloudflare Pages.
#
# Files in public/ are copied to the build output as-is, so this ships with the
# site. Cloudflare reads it at deploy; there is nothing to configure in the
# dashboard.
#
# The desktop app does not use this. It has its own policy, in
# src-tauri/tauri.conf.json, and the two have to be kept in step by hand --
# nothing checks them, and they had drifted badly before anybody compared them
# directive by directive.
#
# They now match except where the platform forces a difference:
#
#   asset:, http://asset.localhost, ipc:, http://ipc.localhost
#       How a Tauri webview reaches local files and the Rust side. Meaningless
#       on the web and absent there.
#
#   script-src
#       Neither has 'unsafe-inline' or 'unsafe-eval' (the desktop's went in
#       2026-10: an injected script there could write anywhere on the disk).
#       The desktop keeps them in devCsp alone, for the dev server's inline
#       hot-reload preamble. accounts.google.com and apis.google.com are the
#       web's alone; the desktop signs in to Google another way.
#
#   img-src/media-src/frame-src http:
#       Plain http is allowed on desktop and not here, where
#       upgrade-insecure-requests rewrites it instead. A hotlinked http image
#       loads in the desktop app and silently does not on the web.

/*
  # Unambiguously safe, so enforced from the start.
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  # The app is never legitimately framed, and saying so is the cheapest
  # defence there is against a clickjacked copy of it.
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  # Nothing here asks for any of these, and an embedded page shouldn't be able
  # to either.
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), camera=(), microphone=(), payment=(), usb=()

  # Enforced. It shipped as Content-Security-Policy-Report-Only first, so that
  # violations showed up in the console without anything being blocked, and was
  # switched over once the real site came back clean.
  #
  # If something here ever needs loosening, put the -Report-Only suffix back
  # before changing the policy rather than after: a wrong CSP is a blank page
  # for every visitor, and this file is served the moment it's pushed.
  #
  # This is defence in depth, not the fix. The holes it would have covered --
  # javascript: URLs reaching an iframe, embeds navigating the top-level window
  # -- are closed in the code itself and don't depend on it.
  #
  #   script-src 'self'         no inline scripts, and no 'unsafe-eval': the
  #                             @pixi/unsafe-eval shim exists so Pixi doesn't
  #                             need it. blob: is for the pdf.js worker.
  #                             'wasm-unsafe-eval' lets WebAssembly compile
  #                             (and nothing else run): the database atriums
  #                             kept in the browser run on (lib/browserPlatform).
  #                             accounts.google.com and apis.google.com: Google
  #                             sign-in for Drive and its Picker (lib/drive).
  #                             Web only; the desktop will sign in otherwise.
  #   style-src 'unsafe-inline' React writes inline style attributes on nearly
  #                             every trace; there is no way around this short
  #                             of rewriting the rendering layer.
  #   img/media https:          traces hotlink images and video from anywhere
  #                             the user pastes, which is the point of them.
  #   frame-src https:          same, for embeds. Can't be a list of hosts.
  #   connect-src https:        "Convert Embeds to Images" downloads the image
  #                             behind an embed, from whatever host it lives on.
  #                             Restricting this to Supabase blocked every one
  #                             of those downloads, and the feature failed on
  #                             every trace. data: is there because ImportAtrium
  #                             fetches its own data: URLs to turn embedded
  #                             files back into blobs. wss://rooms is the
  #                             atrium's room (workers/rooms, lib/rooms).
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' blob: 'wasm-unsafe-eval' https://accounts.google.com https://apis.google.com; worker-src 'self' blob:; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://fonts.googleapis.com https://accounts.google.com/gsi/style; font-src 'self' data: https://fonts.gstatic.com; img-src 'self' data: blob: https:; media-src 'self' data: blob: https:; frame-src https:; connect-src 'self' data: blob: https: wss://rmowxvqkyxypgcbqcspy.supabase.co wss://rooms.digitalatrium.org; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'; frame-ancestors 'none'; upgrade-insecure-requests

# The video relay (public/embed/; see throughRelay in src/lib/embedUrl.ts): the
# one page anything is meant to frame -- the desktop app on macOS and Linux,
# whose pages are tauri://localhost. So the site-wide "never framed" above is
# detached here and replaced by a policy of its own: framed by the app alone,
# running its own script alone, and framing only the video players it names.
/embed/*
  ! X-Frame-Options
  ! Content-Security-Policy
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'none'; script-src 'self'; style-src 'unsafe-inline'; frame-src https://www.youtube.com https://www.youtube-nocookie.com https://player.vimeo.com; frame-ancestors tauri: http://tauri.localhost https://tauri.localhost; base-uri 'none'; form-action 'none'

# The code history: the landing page opens it in a frame over itself, loaded
# ahead so the two can slide past each other (src/lib/codeHistory.ts). Framed
# by this site alone, then, with a policy of its own -- a static page that runs
# its own script and draws on a canvas, and needs nothing else.
# The catalog for AI agents (public/.well-known/ai-catalog.json): JSON, and
# readable from any origin, as the Agentic Resource Discovery spec asks.
/.well-known/ai-catalog.json
  Content-Type: application/json
  Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *

# The agent skill the catalog lists (public/skills/), as Markdown, readable
# from any origin too.
/skills/*
  Content-Type: text/markdown; charset=utf-8
  Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *

/code-history/*
  ! X-Frame-Options
  ! Content-Security-Policy
  X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'none'; script-src 'self'; style-src 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self'; frame-ancestors 'self'; base-uri 'none'; form-action 'none'
